{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 0, "result": {"protocolVersion": "2025-06-18", "capabilities": {"tools": {"listChanged": false}, "resources": {}, "prompts": {}}, "serverInfo": {"name": "ucas", "title": "ucas, a computer algebra system for programmers", "version": "1"}, "instructions": "ucas analyses functions (exhaustively on machine types), does exact algebra and calculus, transforms, number theory and finite fields, and finds cheaper implementations, each answer checked or proved.  Expressions are ucas syntax strings; give parameters types (x: u8, x: f32, x: real) where it matters.  Definitions persist across calls.  An ambiguous input is an error listing its readings: retry with args.assume.KEY.  structuredContent holds the typed result, checks and proof."}}
{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 1, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "  ucas: it(x) = x^2\n  ucas: parity it\nparity of it:\n  even: f(-x) = f(x)\n  proved symbolically (parity rules: x is odd; sums keep a common parity, products multiply it; sin/tan/atan preserve it, cos/abs make it even)\n"}], "structuredContent": {"id": 1, "ok": true, "cmd": "english", "ucas": "is x squared even?", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "english", "statements": ["it(x) = x^2", "parity it"], "understood": true, "results": [{"kind": "parity", "even": "f(-x) = f(x)", "proved_symbolically_parity_rules": "x is odd; sums keep a common parity, products multiply it; sin/tan/atan preserve it, cos/abs make it even)", "headline": "parity of it:"}]}, "notes": [{"kind": "assumed", "text": "\"even\": an even function, f(-x) = f(x) (args.assume.question)"}], "conditions": [], "checks": [], "files": [], "text": "  ucas: it(x) = x^2\n  ucas: parity it\nparity of it:\n  even: f(-x) = f(x)\n  proved symbolically (parity rules: x is odd; sums keep a common parity, products multiply it; sin/tan/atan preserve it, cos/abs make it even)\n"}, "isError": false}}
